From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-1-0082: add bounded holder-space candidate index

Extend the holder-owned RenderProgram with one immutable conservative spatial
candidate index. Keep the unified executor disabled, so this revision cannot
change destination pixels.

Avoid normal-page overhead by admitting the index only after 4096 commands.
At admission, scan only that bounded prefix once; subsequent objects are added
during the existing parser append operation. Use the holder's stable page-space
bounds and a fixed 32x32 grid. Store ordered command indices rather than copied
geometry or page-object pointers. Path bounds proven finite and contained enter
grid postings. Non-path, empty, non-finite, out-of-holder, and broad commands
enter an always-replay stream and can never be culled.

Cap postings at 4,194,304, always-replay commands at 1,048,576, bin coverage at
64 bins per command, and query output at the caller's explicit limit. Any build
or query overflow fails closed to full replay. Query requires the live holder
bounds to match the immutable index bounds, appends into caller-owned reusable
storage, then sorts and deduplicates to restore original painter order without
scanning the complete command stream or allocating auxiliary containers.

Retain no index for small holders or invalid holder bounds. Keep canonical
PDFium as the sole pixel owner established by 0081; 0083 will be the first
revision allowed to consume candidates after complete pre-draw validation.
